In fact it is even worse: when you are restoring a save file, there are also
at most 60 level files created - that amounts to another 750k...

A while ago, a friend of mine posted some changes to compress save files
by a factor of ~50%. A while before, someone else posted something alike to
comp.sources.amiga. The compression method also reduces the size of level
files and bones files. The changes are implemented on an atari ST and a
sinclair QL and it really works great - it even speeds up saving and
restoring a bit.

So, perhaps compression is the answer.
